# Semantic role of a register in a charger register table.
# Readable roles use the documented KEBA P30 value semantics; units in
# canonical form (currents mA, voltages V, power W, energies Wh) after
# applying the per-register offset and scale factor.
# All writable roles must come after Set Charging Current, see
# charger_modbus_tcp.h is_writable_role().
None
Charging State // 0 startup, 1 not ready, 2 ready, 3 charging, 4 error, 5 suspended
Cable State // 0 none, 1/3 cable at station, 5 at vehicle, 7 at vehicle and locked
Error Code // 0 = no error
Current L1 // mA
Current L2 // mA
Current L3 // mA
Voltage L1 // V
Voltage L2 // V
Voltage L3 // V
Active Power // W
Total Energy // Wh
Session Energy // Wh
Max Charging Current // mA, currently active limit of the charger
Max Supported Current // mA, hardware limit of the charger
Phase Switching State // 1 or 3
Serial Number
Firmware Version
Set Charging Current // mA
Set Enabled // 0 disable, 1 enable
Trigger Phase Switch // 0 = one phase, 1 = three phases
Phase Switch Source // 3 = Modbus
Failsafe Current // mA
Failsafe Timeout // seconds, 0 = disabled
Failsafe Persist // 1 = persist
Unlock Plug // 0 = unlock
Set Energy Limit // Wh
